---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base title="Disclosure" description="How AI is used on The Voyager, and other disclosures.">
	<article class="prose">
		<p class="eyebrow">Disclosure</p>
		<h1>Disclosure</h1>
		<p><em>Last updated: 20 October 2026.</em></p>

		<h2 id="ai">How we use AI</h2>
		<p>
			The <a href="/brief/">Daily Brief</a> and the <a href="/deep-dives/">Deep Dives</a> are researched and
			drafted by AI routines that run each morning and publish automatically. Each one ends with a short line saying so.
		</p>
		<ul>
			<li>The routines work from primary sources: release notes, papers, repositories and official documentation.</li>
			<li>Every claim in the brief links to where it came from, and numbers are checked against those sources before publishing.</li>
			<li>A day with nothing worth your time in a section stays empty rather than being filled.</li>
		</ul>
		<p>
			AI can still get things wrong, so check anything important at the source before you rely on it. If you spot a mistake,
			<a href="/contact/">tell me</a> and it will be corrected.
		</p>
		<p>
			Daily Briefs are marked so search engines don't index them, because they mostly point to other people's work. Deep Dives are indexed.
		</p>
		<p>
			These posts are for learning, and they never go out in the newsletter.
		</p>
		<p>
			Posts in <a href="/writing/">Writing</a> and <a href="/projects/">Projects</a> are written by me. The
			newsletter only carries my own writing.
		</p>

		<h2>Opinions</h2>
		<p>
			Everything here is my personal view. It doesn't represent any employer, past or present.
		</p>

		<h2>Advertising</h2>
		<p>
			The site may show ads from Google AdSense. Ads are clearly separate from the posts, and they never
			influence what is written or which sources are used. See the <a href="/privacy/">privacy page</a> for
			how advertising cookies work and how to opt out.
		</p>

		<h2>Affiliate links and sponsorships</h2>
		<p>
			There are none right now. If that ever changes, affiliate links and sponsored content will be clearly
			marked where they appear, and listed on this page.
		</p>
	</article>
</Base>
